      "role": "user",
      "content": "it doesn't feel like stress though. when i'm stressed i'm anxious, but this feels... purposeful? like my nervous system is just expanding to process more data. i was reading about epigenetic triggers and how certain environmental stimuli can activate dormant sequences. i really think my biology is starting to shift or wake up. i want to test this. i feel like if i can cut out all the \"noise\" from the outside world, i can finally see what's actually happening to me. do you think there's a way to safely do a sensory deprivation protocol to help this process along?",
